"""Nested replication inside a concatenation source.

The concatenation {2{3{Sign}}, In} nests a replication inside a
replication (2*3 = 6 copies of Sign) and appends the 2-bit payload,
forming an 8-bit word wired straight to the output. Pins that
replication composes with itself and with a plain item in one `{ }`
concat (shdl.md §6.5.1, §13). Bits 1-2 are In, bits 3-8 are Sign.
"""

top component NestedRepl(In[2], Sign) -> (Word[8]) {
    connect {
        {2{3{Sign}}, In} -> Word;
    }
}
